                    {
                      "type": "markdown",
                      "content": "{% set e = 'sensor.energyhub_ahm_weather_buffer' %}\n{% set auto = is_state('binary_sensor.energyhub_battery_reserve_auto', 'on') %}\n{% set ready = state_attr(e, 'recommendation_status') == 'ready' %}\n{% set deficit = state_attr(e, 'forecast_deficit') %}\n{% set severe = state_attr(e, 'severe_forecast_deficit') %}\n{% set grid = state_attr(e, 'grid_confidence') %}\n{% set grid_name = {'normal':'Normal','unstable':'Unstable','risk':'Risk','panic':'Critical'}.get(grid, 'Unknown') %}\n{% set warnings = state_attr(e, 'qualifying_weather_warning_count') | int(0) %}\n{{ '🤖' if auto else '👥' }} **Battery Reserve Auto: {{ 'ON — EH manages' if auto else 'OFF — manual; EH recommends' }}**\n\n{% if auto %}**Current reserve:** {{ states('input_number.ahm_minimum_soc') }}%\n{% else %}**Selected reserve:** {{ states('input_number.ahm_minimum_soc') }}%\n**EH recommendation:** {{ state_attr(e, 'recommended_soc') if ready else 'Insufficient evidence' }}{{ '%' if ready else '' }}\n{% endif %}**Calculation:** base 20% · generation: {{ 'severe deficit' if severe == true else 'deficit' if deficit == true else 'sufficient' if deficit == false else 'unknown' }} (+{{ state_attr(e, 'generation_modifier_percent') }}%) · Grid Confidence: {{ grid_name }} (+{{ state_attr(e, 'grid_modifier_percent') }}%) · weather: {{ warnings if warnings else 'none' }} (+{{ state_attr(e, 'weather_modifier_percent') }}%) · Smart Heating (+{{ state_attr(e, 'smart_heating_modifier_percent') | default(0) }}%)\n\n**Forecast / consumption average:** {{ state_attr(e, 'solar_forecast_kwh') }} / {{ state_attr(e, 'consumption_average_kwh') if state_attr(e, 'consumption_average_kwh') is not none else 'Unavailable' }} kWh · {{ state_attr(e, 'consumption_sample_count') }} day(s)\n**Forecast plan:** {{ 'preliminary next-day plan' if state_attr(e, 'forecast_plan_stage') == 'preliminary' else '05:00 morning plan' if state_attr(e, 'forecast_plan_stage') == 'morning' else 'waiting' }} for {{ state_attr(e, 'date') }}. Grid and weather are monitored continuously.\n{% set issues = state_attr(e, 'evidence_issues') or [] %}{% if issues %}⚠️ Automatic changes paused: {{ issues | join(', ') }}.{% endif %}"
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "markdown",
                      "title": "Overload Protection",
                      "content": "{% set e = 'sensor.energyhub_peak_load_guard' %}\n{% set requested = is_state('input_boolean.energyhub_load_control_armed', 'on') %}\n{% set supported = state_attr(e, 'mode') in ['automatic', 'warnings_only'] %}\n{% set ready = state_attr(e, 'control_ready') == true %}\n{% set cycle = state_attr(e, 'cycle') or {} %}\n**Automatic switching:** {{ 'ON' if requested else 'OFF — Telegram warnings only' }}\n**Effective control:** {{ 'Available (device checks still apply)' if requested and ready else 'Not ready — no new commands' if requested else 'No new switching commands' }}\n**Status:** {{ states(e) | replace('_', ' ') }}\n{% if not supported %}⚠️ Waiting for the updated EnergyHub app. Do not enable automatic control yet.{% endif %}\n**Load:** {{ states('sensor.powmr_10_2m_load') }}%\n**Thresholds:** 85% trigger · 75% relief · below 50% for five minutes before restoration.\n**Eligible devices:** {{ (state_attr(e, 'eligible_loads') or []) | count }} / 6; fresh readings and verified device state required; no watt allowance setup.\n\n**Devices EH switched OFF:**\n{% for key, owner in cycle.get('owned', {}).items() %}- {{ key | replace('_', ' ') }} · {{ owner.confirmed_off_at }}\n{% else %}None.\n{% endfor %}\nOFF pauses new actions; it does not restore devices immediately or discard ownership. ON restores one at a time, at least one minute apart, with fresh readings below 50%, minimum off time and reserve permission. Missing data pauses restoration; after five minutes Telegram asks the family to check. Family and scheduled OFF requests are respected.\n{% if state_attr(e, 'fault') %}⚠️ {{ state_attr(e, 'fault') }} — manual review required.{% endif %}\n{% for key, reason in cycle.get('blocked', {}).items() %}⚠️ {{ key }}: {{ reason }}\n{% endfor %}\n**Order:** water pump → boiler → first-floor HP (native) → second-floor HP → third-floor HP → microwave.\nThis switch is separate from Battery Reserve Auto. Inverter hardware protection remains independent."
                    },
                    {
                      "type": "markdown",
